[ti:Day 16]

[00:00.00]anti-subsidy [ˌæntɪˈsʌbsədi]a. 反补贴的 例 The United States will still use traditional trade remedies such as anti-dumping and anti-subsidy laws to correct distortions of trade.
[00:18.00]contour [ˈkɒntʊə(r)]n. 轮廓；轮廓线，周线；概要 a. 显 示轮廓的 例 The truly refreshing and unique contour and trapezium design adds a modern touch to your bathroom. 搭 contour line 等高线，轮廓线
[00:35.16]enhance [ɪnˈhɑːns]vt. 提高，加强 例 The practical experience in a large company will enhance your chances of getting a good job.
[00:47.52]trudge [trʌdʒ]vi. 跋涉；步履艰难地走，费力地走 n. 跋 涉；艰难的步行 例 We have to trudge through the snow to the bank.
[00:57.00]user-friendly [ˌjuːzə(r)ˈfrendli]a. 方便用户的 例 The system is user-friendly.
[01:04.80]catalogue [ˈkætəlɒɡ]n. 目录；产品条目；货物价目表；大 学课程一览 vt. 把…编入目录 搭 a catalogue of 一连串；一系列
[01:13.20]transshipment [trænsˈʃɪpmənt]n. 转运(货物)；转载
[01:17.88]immune [ɪˈmjuːn]a. 被豁免的，免除的；不受影响的 例 The employment rate is not immune to economic recession.
[01:27.48]horizon [həˈraɪzn]n. 地平线；范围，界限；[pl.]眼界 例 Reading broadens your horizons, giving you access to new perspectives and ideas. 搭 broaden one's horizons 开阔眼界 / on the horizon (事件)即将来临的，已露端倪的
[01:46.56]thumb [θʌm]n. 拇指；免费搭车 v. 用拇指翻查；〈口〉 竖起拇指要求免费搭车 搭 bite the thumb at sb. 对着某人咬指头(表蔑 视) / by thumb 以免费搭车方式
[01:56.76]blossom [ˈblɒsəm]vi. 兴旺；健康发展 n. 发达期，兴旺期 例 The industry can blossom over night if you find an outlet for new products. 搭 blossom into 发展成；成长为
[02:10.80]crucial [ˈkruːʃl]a. 至关重要的，决定性的；严酷的 例 With the right products and the right terms, these workers can still have access to that crucial crutch. 搭 be crucial to 对…来说是至关重要的 / crucial factor 决定性因素 / crucial issue 重大问题
[02:32.16]finish [ˈfɪnɪʃ]vt. 使破产 vi. 终结；终止关系 n. 完成，结 束；完美 例 The 17-year affiliation between Liverpool and Carlsberg will finish at the end of the current season. 搭 finish off 结束，完成；毁灭 / finish up with 以…结束 / from start to finish 从始至终
[02:54.24]cordial [ˈkɔːdjəl]a. 热忱的，诚恳的；由衷的；深切的； 强心的；刺激的 例 The two sides exchanged in-depth opinions on bilateral relations and other issues of common concern in a cordial and friendly atmosphere.
[03:13.44]recourse [rɪˈkɔːs]n. 求援，求助；追索权 搭 have recourse to 求助于；诉诸或求取(令人不 愉快的手段)
[03:20.88]sophisticated [səˈfɪstɪkeɪtɪd]a. 久经世故的；精致的；复杂的； 尖端的，先进的
[03:27.12]distribution [ˌdɪstrɪˈbjuːʃn]n. 分销；分配；散布；分布 例 The upcoming conference will discuss the fair distribution of wealth and income. 搭 equal distribution of 平均分配…派 distribute v. 分销；分配；散布；分布(例：unfairly distributing affordable housing 经济适用房分配 不公) / distributor n. 批发商，分销商(例：sole distributor 独家经销商)
[03:57.72]unauthorised [ʌnˈɔːθəraɪzd]a. 未被授权的；未经认可的
[04:02.40]confer [kənˈfɜː(r)]v. 商谈，商议；授予；赋予 例 The new corporate leaders often fly to Washington to confer with government officials on national policy. 搭 confer a title on sb. 授予某人一个称号 / confer with sb. on sth. 与某人商谈某事
[04:23.40]impede [ɪmˈpiːd]vt. 阻碍，妨碍，阻止 例 Don't impede your career development with these trivial things.
[04:33.24]tally [ˈtæli]n. 账；记账；理货，计数 vt. 计算，记录 vi. 符合，吻合 例 The bag I have received does not tally with the sample on-line. 搭 buy on/upon tally 赊账
[04:46.56]alongside [əˌlɒŋˈsaɪd]ad. 在旁边 prep. 在…旁边 例 Alongside an explanation of the sources of firm differentials, there must also be an explanation of the mechanism.
[05:02.64]unparalleled [ʌnˈpærəleld]a. 无比的；空前的 搭 unparalleled in history 史无前例的
[05:09.96]quantum [ˈkwɒntəm]n. 量；定额；份额；总额；数量 例 He provided everyone with the same quantum of free gifts.
[05:19.68]divulge [daɪˈvʌldʒ]vt. 泄露；透露 例 None of those clearinghouses would divulge the members of their risk committees. 搭 divulge secret 泄露秘密
[05:33.36]shareholding [ˈʃeəhəʊldɪŋ]n. 持股；股权
[05:37.20]sight [saɪt]a. 见票即付的；即期的
[05:39.84]automate [ˈɔːtəmeɪt]v. (使)自动化；自动操作；把自动化技 术应用于 例 There are some great products out there that can automate this process.
[05:52.20]define [dɪˈfaɪn]vt. 给…下定义；限定，规定；明确表示 例 It is urgent for the government to define its trade relationship with the European Union clearly. 搭 define sb's duty 规定某人的任务 / define sb's position 表明某人的立场 ex-dividend 无股息
[06:13.68]mercenary [ˈmɜːsənəri]a. 唯利是图的；雇佣的 n. 佣工；雇 佣兵 搭 mercenary marriage 买卖婚姻 / mercenary troop 雇佣军
[06:23.28]collide [kəˈlaɪd]vi. 碰撞；冲突，抵触 vt. 使碰撞 例 We know that more is to be gained when great powers cooperate than when they collide. 搭 collide with sth./sb. 与…发生冲突
[06:38.88]coalition [ˌkəʊəˈlɪʃn]n. 联合；联盟 例 The coalition government sees this as a way of delegating power and strengthening localism.
[06:51.72]policyholder [ˈpɒləsihəʊldə(r)]n. 保险客户；投保人
[06:56.52]scupper [ˈskʌpə(r)]vt. 使毁坏；突袭；消灭；击败 例 They worry that the new demands might scupper the whole deal.
[07:06.72]overhaul [ˌəʊvəˈhɔːl]vt. 彻底检查，大修；彻底革新；追上 并超过 [ˈəʊvəhɔːl]n. 彻底检查，大修；彻底改革 例 It is general ly appreciated that the government plans to overhaul financial regulations this year. 搭 overhaul of the school curriculum 学校课程 改革
[07:29.28]endorse [ɪnˈdɔːs]vt. 在(票据)背面签名，背书；(为商品等) 担保 例 The cheque is endorsed. 搭 endorse over 背书(支票等)转让权利
[07:39.36]boutique [buːˈtiːk]n. 时装用品小商店；流行女装商店；精 品店；(小型)专业公司 例 The company now lets you add the number of whatever you want at their new online boutique.
[07:54.00]bond [bɒnd]n. 契约；债券；保税单；付款保证书；保 证金 vt. 以…作抵押；为…作担保 例 Issuing more government bonds is an expansionary monetary policy.
[08:06.36]monetary [ˈmʌnɪtri]a. 货币的；金钱的；财政的
[08:10.08]demanding [dɪˈmɑːndɪŋ]a. 要求高的 例 The job he introduced to me is much too demanding for me.
[08:18.96]retirement [rɪˈtaɪəmənt]n. 退休，退职；引退
[08:22.92]convince [kənˈvɪns]vt. 使确信；使信服，说服 例 How can I convince my boss to invest in our ideas? 搭 be convinced of 确信 / convince sb. of sth. 使某人相信某事
[08:36.48]autonomous [ɔːˈtɒnəməs]a. 自治的；独立自主的；自主的 例 Each team should be autonomous except in matters affecting other teams or the organisation as a whole. 搭 autonomous region 自治区
[08:53.76]overwhelm [ˌəʊvəˈwelm]v. 覆盖；淹没；压倒；击垮 例 The country fears that giant multinational firms will overwhelm its domestic enterprises.
[09:07.32]clipboard [ˈklɪpbɔːd]n. 剪贴板 例 In a series of experiments, study participants were asked to answer questionnaires that were attached to a metal clipboard.
[09:23.04]eloquent [ˈeləkwənt]a. 雄辩的，有说服力的 例 The chief negotiator is tough and eloquent.
