[12:15.12]hypocrisy [hɪˈpɒkrəsi]n. 伪善，虚伪 例 The growing protectionist sentiment in the US is particularly noisome because it reeks of so much hypocrisy.
[12:29.64]appalling [əˈpɔːlɪŋ]a. 骇人听闻的；极糟的；很严重的 例 Everyone could not help but notice the absolutely appalling physical conditions and the oppressive atmosphere. 搭 appalling crime 骇人听闻的罪行
[12:48.12]gilt-edged [ˌɡɪltˈedʒd]a. 金边的；最上等的，最高质量或价 值的 例 The inflation-linked bonds are among the gilt-edged ones, and are often regarded as risk-free.
[13:02.88]expenditure [ɪkˈspendɪtʃə(r)]n. 经费，支出额；(时间、金钱 等的)花费，支出 例 As for an international company, the business travel is a big part of the overhead expenditure. 搭 revenue and expenditure 岁入和岁出，收支
