[13:30.12]outsource [ˈaʊtsɔːs]vt. 把…外包；外购 例 They decided to outsource some projects to other small companies for financial reasons.
[13:42.72]amortisation [əˌmɔːtaɪˈzeɪʃn]n. 摊销，摊还；分期偿付 例 Free cash flow is a broader measure that takes earnings and adds depreciation and amortisation while subtracting capital expenditures.
[14:01.56]offer [ˈɒfə(r)]v. 出价 n. 报盘；发盘；出价，报价；主 动提议，建议 例 All of this merchandise is on offer. 搭 on offer (削价)销售 / under offer (指代售房 屋)已有人出价的
[14:14.52]consensus [kənˈsensəs]n. 集体意见，君子协定；(意见等) 一致 例 The whole of society should arrive at the consensus that wealth is not the hallmark of social status, but individual virtues and ethics are. 搭 consensus of opinion 意见一致 / reach a consensus on 在…上达成一致意见
[14:39.48]radiant [ˈreɪdiənt]a. 辐射的；光芒四射的
