[14:54.72]muddle [ˈmʌdl]n. 糊涂；混乱 vt. 弄乱，弄糟；糊里糊涂 打发；浪费 vi. 胡乱对待；混日子 例 Tell me the truth and don't muddle me around! 搭 muddle along/on 胡乱进行；得过且过
[15:08.04]facelift [ˈfeɪslɪft]vt. 翻新；整容 n. 改建；翻新；整容 例 The building projects are not just a way of giving the city a facelift; they also keep people in work.
[15:22.56]dubious [ˈdjuːbiəs]a. 怀疑的；犹豫不决的，无把握的； 靠不住的；含糊的 例 Those figures alone are a dubious basis for such a conclusion. 搭 be dubious of 对…怀疑的；对…无把握的
